; KEYBOARD.DEF - the layouts in KEYBOARD.SYS.  UTF-8.
;
; TOOLS\MKNLS.PS1 turns this into NLS\KEYBOARD.ASM, which BUILD.CMD
; assembles into KEYBOARD.SYS.  Run the script after changing a line.
;
; A section is one layout: [code id] and a name.  The code is what
; KEYB takes; the id tells two layouts of one country apart
; (KEYB IT,,/ID:142), and the first section with a code is the one
; KEYB loads when no id is given.
;
;   cp     the code pages the layout is made for.  A character a page
;          does not have is a key that types nothing in that page
;   E D C B    the four rows of typing keys as they are on the board,
;          left to right, one character a key:
;            E  the key left of 1, the digits, and the two after 0
;            D  Q to P, and the two after P
;            C  A to L, the two after L, and the key beside Enter
;            B  the key between the left Shift and Z (the 102nd key),
;               Z to M, and the three after M
;          with no mark the keys alone, + with Shift, @ with AltGr
;          (the right Alt, or Ctrl and Alt), @+ with AltGr and Shift.
;          The sign for "nothing here" is the empty set, U+2205.
;   dead   the positions that are dead keys: the row, the key counted
;          as the standards count it (E00 is the key left of 1, D01 is
;          Q, C01 is A, B00 is the 102nd key, B01 is Z) and the level.
;          The accent is the character at that position
;   caps   the keys Caps Lock shifts
;   dec    what the keypad's decimal key types
;
; The sections were drafted with TOOLS\KBDDUMP.PS1 from the layouts
; Windows has for the same national keyboards.  What Windows added
; later - the euro sign - is in none of these code pages and so types
; nothing.

